        "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ compute $P(Z\\ge 0.37).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ | $\\,0.6406\\,$ | $\\,0.6443\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6736\\,$ | $\\,0.6772\\,$ | $\\,0.6808\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ | $\\,0.7123\\,$ | $\\,0.7157\\,$ |",
        "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z\\ge 0.37).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/020f8a79730152c5c283dc8939e58f9ec44cf93b9f6727822df9de7447af8f5c.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge 0.37) & =1-P(Z<0.37) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(0.37)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/20c48d96e4941259d89303bdbfadd92125ad155bc068836ddeb510b655ec19a6.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\u03a6(0.37)=0.6443.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge 0.37) & =1-\u03a6(0.37) \\\\  & =1-0.6443 \\\\  & =0.3557.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
